body:
Hi, 

I would like to retrieve a list of objects for a defined category. 

For this I tested two methods:

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch({
    [...],
    searchParameters: {
      hierarchicalFacetsRefinements: {
        'categories.fr.0': {
          0: 'Revêtement > Éléments de décor > Poignées de portes'
        }
      }
    }
  });
```

This returns me an error message: _Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'facets' of undefined_

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch({
    [...],
    searchParameters: {
      facetsRefinements: {
        'categories.fr.0': {
          0: 'Revêtement'
        }
      }
    }
  });
```

It works just for a level 1 category .. In my case "Revêtement", then I want to pass it "Revêtement > Éléments de décor > Poignées de portes"

How to do ? An idea ?

comments.body:
Hi @vvo, sorry for the response time too.
Indeed, for my product index , I have a facet 'categories.fr.0 ' and use a hierarchical widget instantsearch for the categories . So I wanted to have a page listing products with a category selected during initialization.
Finaly, the algolia support gave me the solution:

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch({
  [...],
  searchParameters: {
    hierarchicalFacetsRefinements: {
      'categories.fr.0': ['Revêtement > Éléments de décor > Poignées de portes']
    }
  }
});
```
